{"name":"Fireplace Kitten","hex":"#c5c9c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fireplace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An open hearth for holding a fire at the base of a chimney."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireplace"},{"term":"kitten","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young cat, especially before sexual maturity (reached at about seven months).","A young rabbit, rat, hedgehog, squirrel, fox, beaver, badger, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give birth to kittens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitten"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fireplace","blocks":[{"text":"A fireplace or hearth is a structure made of brick, stone or metal designed to contain a fire. Fireplaces are used to heat a room or dwelling and also for the relaxing ambiance they create. Modern fireplaces vary in heat efficiency, depending on the design."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Open_fireplace_with_icon.jpg/330px-Open_fireplace_with_icon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireplace"},{"title":"Kitten","blocks":[{"text":"A kitten is a juvenile cat. After being born, kittens display primary altriciality and are fully dependent on their mothers for survival. They normally do not open their eyes for seven to ten days. After about two weeks, kittens develop quickly and begin to explore the world beyond their nest. After a further three to four weeks, they begin to eat solid food and grow baby teeth. Domestic kittens are highly social animals and usually enjoy human companionship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Juvenile_Ragdoll.jpg/330px-Juvenile_Ragdoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitten"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Outdoor_Firepla